<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="63286" href="schedule/2016/spring/HCD/595/63286.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2016" href="schedule/2016.xml">2016</calendarYear><term id="120161" href="schedule/2016/spring.xml">Spring 2016</term><subject id="HCD" href="schedule/2016/spring/HCD.xml">Human and Community Development</subject><course id="595" href="schedule/2016/spring/HCD/595.xml">Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>GFW</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Gender Perspectives Fam &amp; Work</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 19-Jan-16 - 11-Mar-16.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Family and work are two life domains that are central to most individuals and families. In this seminar we will focus on the intersection of family and work and how bargining, exchange, and gendered roles play out in shaping family division of paid and unpaid work, family-work conflict, marital satisfaction and other outcomes. Each week, a different student will lead discussion in class on a different research topic that relates to the intersection of family and work.</sectionText><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2016-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2016-03-11Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>108</roomNumber><buildingName>Bevier Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Kramer" firstName="K">Kramer, K</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>